    "lastText": "All eight issues in ISSUES.md are fixed, and `npm test` passes (17 tests, 0 failures).\n\n- **#1 `wordWrap`:** lines never exceed `width`. Long words are cut into `width`-sized pieces, and there are no empty lines at the start or end. Paragraphs are wrapped separately and joined by one blank line, and single newlines count as spaces.\n- **#2 `truncate`:** it counts code points, so emoji stay whole. The ellipsis counts toward `max`, and whitespace before it is removed. A custom `ellipsis` works.\n- **#3 CSV:** `parseCSVLine` handles quoted commas, `\"\"` escapes and empty fields. I added `parseCSV`, which handles `\\r\\n` and line breaks inside quotes and ignores a trailing newline. It is exported through `src/index.js` automatically.\n- **#4 and #5 `formatTable`:** the column count is the longest row, and missing cells are treated as empty. Numeric columns are right-aligned, `{ header: true }` adds the separator line and ignores the header row when detecting numbers, and lines have no trailing spaces.\n- **#6 `pluralize`:** it handles vowel+`y`, consonant+`y`, `s`/`x`/`z`/`ch`/`sh`, the seven irregular nouns, capitalisation, and singular only for counts 1 and -1.\n- **#7 `render`:** `{{ }}` escapes HTML and `{{{ }}}` does not. Dotted paths, `|default` and spaces inside the braces work, and missing values render as an empty string.\n- **#8 `levenshtein`:** empty strings return the other string's length. It accepts `ignoreCase` and `maxDistance`, and stops early once the distance exceeds `maxDistance`.\n\nI added `test/issues.test.js` with checks for the examples from the issues.\n\nA row shorter than the others keeps its column separators: `formatTable([['a','b','c'],['d']])` gives `d |   |`. I read \"missing cells are treated as empty strings\" that way, so the separators stay even though trailing spaces are trimmed.",
